course: dictionary
lesson: 11002
title: Waste: rubbish, or using too much
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word waste can mean different things, and the words around it show which one. «Rubbish goes in the right bin: recycling, compost or general waste.» Here waste means rubbish, things thrown away because nobody wants them.
explain: Waste can also be a verb, meaning to use more than you need, or to use something for nothing. «Growing food and making clothes also uses a great deal of water, so wasting food wastes water too.» Wasting food means using up food that is then thrown away, so the water used to grow it is used for nothing.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Never pretend to be hurt as a joke; it can waste emergency services' time.» If you put "use up for nothing" in place of waste and it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Waste can be a noun (the rubbish itself) or a verb (to use something badly or for nothing).
fact: «Waste» as a noun means rubbish: things thrown away because they are not wanted.
fact: «A waste of time» means time used for nothing useful.
fact: «To waste» means to use more than you need, or to use something for nothing.
fact: «Waste land» is land that is empty and not used.
exercise: «Rubbish goes in the right bin: recycling, compost or general waste.» What is waste in this sentence? | *Things thrown away because they are not wanted | A kind of bin | Money saved for later
exercise: In «wasting food wastes water too», what does wasting mean? | Cooking dinner for the family | *Using more than you need, or using something for nothing | Growing food on a farm | Putting food in a bin for recycling
exercise: A tap wastes 3 litres of water each day. How much water is wasted in 5 days? | *15 litres | 8 litres | 53 litres | 2 litres
test: «Never pretend to be hurt as a joke; it can waste emergency services' time.» What does waste mean here? | *To use up time for nothing | To throw rubbish in a bin | To be empty and not used | To grow food
test: «Reducing waste helps most, because the waste is never made.» What does waste mean in this sentence? | Land that is empty | *Rubbish that is thrown away | Using more than you need | A type of bin
exam: Which phrase means time used for nothing useful? | Waste paper | Waste water | Waste bin | *A waste of time
